		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>Mispronunciation detection at the phoneme level provides detailed feedback for Quranic reciters. Standard speech-to-text models cannot capture subtle differences in letter pronunciation; thus, developing a speech-to-phoneme system is essential. Prior works have mainly explored encoder-only models. In this work, we adapt Whisper-large-v3 on the IqraEval dataset. Our experimental results show that the proposed system achieved an F1score of 0.3224, an accuracy of 0.6894, and a high recall of 0.7624. These results highlight promising directions for further research and development in phoneme-level mispronunciation detection.</p>
			</abstract>
